  Your data-sharing doubt is a real flaw in the locked design

  Decision 11 says dev, stage and uat can read prod data "via PostgreSQL GRANTs". That cannot work as written.

  - Dev, stage and uat run on the non-prod database. Prod runs on the prod database. They are separate Cloud SQL instances in separate projects.
  - A PostgreSQL GRANT only works between schemas on the same instance. It cannot cross instances.
  - The two obvious workarounds both break the design:
    - A read replica of prod copies the whole instance, so it holds every customer's data. That breaks customer isolation, and it puts prod data in non-prod.
    - A cross-database link (postgres_fdw) needs a network path and a stored credential from non-prod into prod. That breaks the "no prod credentials in non-prod"
      rule.

  BigQuery and GCS don't have this problem, because their access control is cross-project IAM.

  Proposal: share by data type

  ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────┐
  │                    Data                     │                               How other environments get it                                │  Live or copy  │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┤
  │ Shared reference data (catalogs, configs,   │ Stored in GCS or BigQuery, not in Cloud SQL. All of the customer's environments read it    │ Live read, no  │
  │ feature flags)                              │ with IAM.                                                                                  │ copy           │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┤
  │ Analytics data (BigQuery)                   │ Non-prod reads prod through authorized views and row-level policies. The views can         │ Live read      │
  │                                             │ anonymize.                                                                                 │                │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┤
  │ Files (GCS)                                 │ The same bucket, with prefix IAM per environment. Cross-project access is allowed by a     │ Live read      │
  │                                             │ VPC-SC ingress rule for that customer only.                                                │                │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┤
  │ Relational data (Cloud SQL)                 │ Not a live read. Non-prod gets a sanitized copy from the tenant-scoped export/import, run  │ Copy,          │
  │                                             │ weekly or on demand.                                                                       │ sanitized      │
  ├─────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────┤
