● Agreed. Every prod cell gets both HA and DR by default. Multi-region is no longer an opt-in.

  - HA: survive a zone failure, inside the region, automatically.
  - DR: survive a region failure by failing over to a paired region.

  1. Region pairs

  Each prod region has a fixed DR partner in the same jurisdiction, so data residency still holds:

  # clusters/regions.yaml
  - name: us-east1
    drPair: us-central1
  - name: europe-west1
    drPair: europe-west4

  When a prod region is added, L2 creates both regions together. A prod region without its DR pair can't go active.

  2. Default prod design: HA in-region, warm standby DR

  ┌───────────────┬────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │   Component   │         HA (zone failure)          │                                         DR (region failure)                                          │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ GKE           │ Regional cluster, 3 zones, PDBs    │ DR cluster in the pair region, running at minimum size. ArgoCD deploys every prod app to it too, at  │
  │               │                                    │ minimum replicas. It scales up on failover.                                                          │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Cloud SQL     │ Regional HA (synchronous standby,  │ Cross-region read replica, promoted on failover                                                      │
  │               │ automatic failover)                │                                                                                                      │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Cloud Run     │ Multi-zone by default              │ Same service deployed in the pair region, behind the global LB                                       │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ GCS           │ Not applicable                     │ Dual-region buckets across the pair                                                                  │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ BigQuery      │ Not applicable                     │ Cross-region dataset replica, or multi-region location (check what the region pair supports)         │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Pub/Sub       │ Global service                     │ Message storage restricted to the region pair. Subscriptions are re-pointed to the DR Cloud Run on   │
  │               │                                    │ failover.                                                                                            │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ PVCs          │ Regional PD (2 zones)              │ Backup for GKE backups stored in the pair region, restored on failover                               │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Edge          │ Global LB health checks            │ Global LB fails the customer's hostname over to the DR backends                                      │
  ├───────────────┼────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Supporting    │ Not applicable                     │ Secrets replicated to the pair. Artifact Registry is multi-region. KMS keys must exist in both       │
  │ pieces        │                                    │ regions, because a regional Cloud SQL replica needs a key in its own region.                         │
  └───────────────┴────────────────────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  Non-prod stays as before: zonal or regional HA, backup-and-restore, no DR.

  3. Failover happens per cell, not per customer

  Many customers share one Cloud SQL instance (20-40 databases each). A Cloud SQL failover moves the whole instance, so all customers on that cell fail over
  together. Each cluster inventory file records its pair, e.g. drCluster: prod-us-central1-01. A runbook covers failover (promote replica, scale up DR, switch LB)
  and failback.

  4. Targets (proposed, to confirm)

  ┌──────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────┬─────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │               Profile                │      RTO      │     RPO     │                       How                       │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼─────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Zone failure (HA)                    │ About 1-5 min │ 0           │ Automatic                                       │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼─────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Region failure, default warm standby │ About 30 min  │ About 5 min │ Promote replica, scale up DR cluster, switch LB │
  ├──────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────┼─────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ Region failure, opt-in hot standby   │ About 5 min   │ About 1 min │ DR cluster kept at full size                    │
  └──────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────┴─────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  These are design targets, not measured numbers. Replica lag and promotion time must be proven in the quarterly DR tests. The earlier region.secondary opt-in
  becomes the hot-standby option instead.

  5. Cost impact

  - Prod regional footprint roughly doubles in fixed cost. You pay for a second cluster, plus Cloud SQL replicas that must be the same size as the primary to take
    the load.
  - The DR cluster runs small, so compute cost is lower than full duplication.
  - GCS dual-region and cross-region replication add storage and network-egress cost.

  6. What changes in v3

  - Decision 6 rewritten: HA plus warm-standby DR for every prod cell, and hot standby opt-in.
  - regions.yaml gets drPair. The cluster inventory gets drCluster.
  - L2 creates the region pair for prod.
  - The prod ArgoCD deploys to both the primary and DR clusters.
  - Success criteria: prod 99.9% for every customer, RTO and RPO per the table, quarterly failover tests per cell.

